!
! Lines 1-3 are COMMENT CARDS -- a "-" in the NAME column, no
! LOCATION, no BINARY OUTPUT.  The asterisk runs are transcribed as
! read at 400 dpi; their LENGTHS are not claimed to the character,
! because nothing on the page or in the image depends on them and
! counting 64 drum asterisks by eye is not a reading anybody should
! trust.  Line 2's box is "COPY CONTROL WORD", read closed and
! unambiguous.  Line 26 is printed ONE COLUMN FURTHER RIGHT than
! every other statement on the page (" B,KREJT"), which is a
! keypunch artefact of the second statement on card IC000025 and
! changes nothing.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE CHECKS.  Thirty rows, which is EVERY emitting row on the
! page, and six symbols, which is every label the page defines.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!SYM   BCCWR    217766.00
!SYM   B3MCP    217773.00
!SYM   B3TRY    220000.00
!SYM   B3ER1    220005.00
!SYM   KDONE    220006.40
!SYM   B3FAT    220007.40
!CHECK 217766.00 | 000020.02 30 | line 5 B CCW R LV,1,$0 -- 000020 is word 16, which IS index register 0; LV,1,$1 prints 000021.02 30
!CHECK 217766.40 | 215001.04 80 217773.34 02 | line 6 BB,S L,B 3MCP -- the "02" spells BB against BZB's "00" (line 13); .34 is B 3MCP's EVEN half word
!CHECK 217767.40 | 000021.22 80 006000.20 50 | line 7 L(BU,6),$X1+0.18 -- 000021 is word 17 = index register 1; .22 is 18 decimal; 006 is the byte size 6
!CHECK 217770.40 | 220005.34 C0 | line 8 BZRZ,B 3ER1 -- BRZ prints C2; printed p.152 line 14 prints the same C0 for the same mnemonic
!CHECK 217771.00 | 215230.42 90 | line 9 KV,$X1,S TLR+0.32 -- .42 is 0o40 (32 bits) plus J=1's 0o02
!CHECK 217771.40 | 220005.32 42 | line 10 BXL,B3ER1 -- BXH prints .33 (line 12), BXE prints byte C2 (line 15)
!CHECK 217772.00 | 215230.02 90 | line 11 KV,$X1,S TLR -- the same address as line 9 with no bit offset, which is what makes line 9's .42 self-checking
!CHECK 217772.40 | 220005.33 42 | line 12 BXH,B 3ER1
!CHECK 217773.00 | 000000.32 8A 220006.74 00 | line 13 B 3MCP BZB,S CH OP($10),K DONE -- byte A is i1 = $10 = 10 decimal; the trailing 00 spells BZB; .74 is K DONE's ODD half word
!CHECK 217774.00 | 000000.51 04 | line 14 KVI,$4,.32 -- printed "$4"; line 30 prints the same J as a bare "4"
!CHECK 217774.40 | 221065.32 C2 | line 15 BXE,K C BUSY
!CHECK 217775.00 | 000000.37 8B 220007.74 02 | line 16 BB,S SET UP($11),B 3 FAT -- printed as THREE tokens for one six-character name
!CHECK 217776.00 | 000000.47 8B 220007.74 02 | line 17 BB,SSEL($11),B3FAT -- the same target as line 16 with both names closed up
!CHECK 217777.00 | 000003.32 9C | line 18 KV,13,S FI AAC($12) -- .32 is J=13 alone (2*13 = 0o32); byte C is i = $12 = 12 decimal
!CHECK 217777.40 | 220007.72 C0 | line 19 BZXE,B 3FAT -- .72 against line 31's .32 is the half-word bit, and it is the only part of a branch address that shows
!CHECK 220000.00 | 000003.15 02 | line 20 B 3TRY LCI,$X6,3.0 -- .15 is 2*6+1, the immediate-count J encoding
!CHECK 220000.40 | 000000.00 8E 000000.21 01 | line 21 CCW,0.0($14),0.0($1) -- 8E is i1 = $14, 01 is i2 = $1; this LOCATION carries the unexplained second asterisk
!CHECK 220001.40 | 000003.30 8D 001000.06 70 | line 22 LF(BU,1),3.24($13) -- L would print 001000.20 50; .30 is 24 decimal
!CHECK 220002.40 | 000000.30 81 001000.12 F0 | line 23 SF(BU,1),0.24($1) -- ST would print 001000.20 D0
!CHECK 220003.40 | 216242.03 44 | line 24 BZEKJZ,K SUPP -- BZEKJ prints 40, so the trailing Z is read off the bits and not off the ink
!CHECK 220004.00 | 220000.54 48 | line 25 CB,6,B3TRY+.32 -- the .40 bit of the target shows inside the printed .54
!CHECK 220004.40 | 221300.10 00 | line 26 B,KREJT (same card as line 25) -- a plain B prints target+.10
!CHECK 220005.00 | 010010.35 01 | line 27 B 3ER1 LVI,14,S CCW AD -- .35 is 2*14+1, LVI's J encoding; the 010010 is printed p.107's "(16)1008.0" error code
!CHECK 220005.40 | 217451.40 80 | line 28 SIC,S DISIC -- SIC prints the bare 24-bit address, so this row pins S DISIC to the bit
!CHECK 220006.00 | 217372.10 00 | line 29 B,S DISP (same card as line 28; the SIC/branch pair is complete on this page and on ONE card)
!CHECK 220006.40 | 000001.51 04 | line 30 K DONE KVI,4,1.32 -- the same .51 as line 14 with the word address 1 instead of 0
!CHECK 220007.00 | 220000.32 C2 | line 31 BXE,B 3TRY -- .32 is B 3TRY's EVEN half word, against line 19's .72
!CHECK 220007.40 | 000004.00 1D | line 32 B 3FAT LX,0,S CCW($13) -- byte D is i = $13 = 13 decimal
!CHECK 220010.00 | 000000.01 11 | line 33 SX,0,0.0($1) -- byte 1 is i = $1
!CHECK 220010.40 | 216242.10 00 | line 34 B,K SUPP -- a half word, so the counter leaves this page at 220011.00
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE CHECKS DO NOT SHOW
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! 1. THE ORIGIN.  The page prints "SLC,$" and this deck writes a
!    hard SLC.  All thirty !CHECKs would pass at a wrong origin.
!    Closed by hand against printed p.156's last row, against volume
!    OCR 9140's "B,B CCW R" at 217766.10, and against printed
!    p.158's own "220011.00 * SLC,$" -- see THE JOINS.
!
! 2. FOUR EXTERNALS ARE KNOWN ONLY TO THE HALF WORD, because the
!    instruction that references them does not print the bits below
!    bit 32:  K SUPP (lines 24, 34), K C BUSY (line 15), K REJT
!    (line 26), S DISP (line 29) and S CCW AD (line 27, an LVI).
!    S CCW (line 32) likewise, through an LX.  Writing ".0" for
!    those is a CONVENTION, not a reading.  The ones this page DOES
!    pin to the bit are S L, S TLR, S CH OP, S SET UP, S SEL,
!    S FI AAC (all full 24-bit bit addresses in a VFL or
!    branch-on-bit field) and S DISIC (a SIC).
!
! 3. SIX LABELS ARE DEFINED HERE AND FIVE OF THEM ARE REFERENCED
!    NOWHERE ELSE IN THE VOLUME -- B 3MCP, B 3TRY, B 3ER1, B 3FAT
!    and K DONE.  listing_oracle checks locations and bits and never
!    a label's SPELLING, and check_symbol_spellings needs a SECOND
!    deck to compare against.  All five therefore rest on ink alone
!    for their names; their ADDRESSES are pinned by the page's own
!    branches and are in the checked set.  Only B CCW R has an
!    outside witness (volume OCR 9140).  See UNRESOLVED.
!
! 4. THE ASTERISK RUNS on lines 1-3 are not counted to the
!    character.  They emit nothing.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> WHAT I COULD NOT RESOLVE <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (a) "K DONE" -- the D and the O rest on ink and English, with no
!     second reader anywhere.  It is referenced ONLY by line 13 of
!     this page; greps of the whole-volume OCR for "K DONE" and
!     "K CONE" return nothing but this page's own two cards (which
!     the OCR renders "K CCNE", i.e. the OCR gets BOTH glyphs
!     wrong).  The 1800-dpi reading in GLYPHS (2) is as far as shape
!     can go: the first glyph has the straight left stem of a D and
!     the second is a stemless ring.  "K CONE" and "K DOME" are not
!     words; "K DONE" is, and the comments agree.  But no check in
!     this repository can ever catch it, and if the merged image
!     ever gains another page that references it, that page's
!     spelling wins over this one.
!
! (b) "S CCW AD" -- printed p.107's deck records this name as
!     genuinely unresolved among SCCWAD / SCOWAD / SOCWAD, and this
!     page is a second page printing the same name at the same
!     address (010010.00, confirmed to the half word by line 27's
!     LVI).  THIS PAGE READS IT "S CCW AD" -- C, C, W -- at 900 dpi,
!     with the comment "-CW DEST ADDR INVALID" using "CW" for the
!     control word three times on this page.  That is a second
!     INDEPENDENT reader agreeing with p.107's chosen spelling, and
!     it is the strongest thing available, but it is still two
!     readings off the same drum of a name no typeset manual spells.
!     NOT claimed as settled.
!
! (c) "S FI AAC" (line 18) -- printed p.101 defines it, cites
!     Appendix A printed p.269 for the spelling, and that is the
!     spelling taken here.  >>> THIS PAGE ADDS NO INDEPENDENT
!     READING, AND IT IS NOT A DOUBT. <<<  At 900 dpi the final
!     glyph is a stemless open ring with no straight left side and
!     no squared corners, so the C/D discriminator of
!     docs/transcription_workflow.md rules D OUT; and under the
!     drum's one-way asymmetry (dropout OPENS a closed glyph and
!     never closes an open one) an open ring is consistent with a C
!     and with an O but not with a D.  What this page cannot do is
!     distinguish C from O there, which is exactly what p.101's
!     Appendix A citation settles.  Recorded so the next
!     transcriber does not re-open it: the address is checked
!     (000003.00) and the spelling is p.101's.
!
! (d) THE SECOND ASTERISK on lines 4 and 21 is unexplained, and this
!     page widens rather than narrows it (see THE SECOND ASTERISK).
!     No rule proposed.
!
! (e) THE CARD-SERIAL PREFIX CHANGES.  Printed p.152's cards are
!     IA000047..IA000092; this page's are IC000001..IC000032,
!     restarting at 1.  So the deck changes somewhere in printed
!     pp.153-156 and the serials are NOT a continuous count across
!     the volume.  Whether an "IB" block exists, and whether the
!     restart means a separately-assembled section, is not
!     answerable from this page.  It does not affect the
!     within-page argument, which only needs the serials to be
!     consecutive on THIS page, and they are.
